- op: discuss  # fcd2
  at: '2026-08-21T19:05:55Z'  # fcd2
  by: agent  # fcd2
  actor: jgstern_agent  # fcd2
  clock: 4  # fcd2
  nonce: fcd2  # fcd2
  message: "SATISFIED 2026-08-21, PR #465 (dev cb6498171e), on behavioral evidence at the\ncorrect pipeline stage with a built-in discriminator.\n\nWHAT SHIPPED. The per-PR arm's trigger widens from the claim-surface include-list\nto the shared *code_paths anchor (the pytest/lint trigger) plus\ndocs/hypergumbo-self-catalog/**, which holds a README that *code_paths does not\nmatch. The gate now lives in the pipeline the merge path already reads: auto-pr\npolls exactly one context, ci/woodpecker/pr/woodpecker, so a claim regression\nfails the PR that introduces it. Detection is bounded at ONE commit BY\nCONSTRUCTION and depends on no signal delivery at all -- which matters, because\nthe three delivery defects this thread established are not fixable by adding\nanother scheduled arm.\n\nTHE CLOSURE EVIDENCE, and it carries its own discriminator. The widened gate RAN\nON ITS OWN PR. That PR touched exactly four files:\n\n    .ci/affected-tests.txt\n    .woodpecker/woodpecker.yml\n    CHANGELOG.md\n    tests/test_ci_self_claims_gate_scope.py\n\nNOT ONE of them is on the old include-list. Under the trigger this item was filed\nagainst, the gate would not have run on this PR at all. Fetched log for the PR\nhead 7a05f3a99e, job self-claims-gate:\n\n    + PYTHON=python scripts/check-self-claims\n    check-self-claims: analysing hypergumbo with hypergumbo ...\n    check-self-claims-drift: OK -- 18 claims unchanged (18 confirmed_with_caveats).\n\nSo the gate ran, completed, and returned a verdict on a commit the old trigger\nwould have skipped. That is the statement of this item demonstrated, not proxied.\n\nWHY THE GATE CAN ALSO FAIL, stated because a gate observed only passing is\nindistinguishable from one that cannot fail. Four links, each independently\nevidenced rather than assumed: (a) the script's drift path works and reddens a\npipeline -- observed in the 2026-08-19 01:00 cron log, which printed SELF-CLAIM\nDRIFT and named this item's regression; (b) both arms run the IDENTICAL command\nblock -- previously a prose claim in woodpecker.yml with nothing enforcing it,\nnow pinned by test_both_arms_run_the_same_commands; (c) the per-PR arm runs on\nany code change -- (a) above, observed; (d) auto-pr may permit a merge only on a\nzero verdict -- pinned by tests/test_ci_verdict_default_deny.py (WI-ditav).\n\nTHE TRADE WAS RE-PRICED, NOT OVERRULED. The claim-surface scoping was a\ndeliberate decision recorded at woodpecker.yml, priced there at \"~10 minutes\" per\nPR. Measured on dev 6e290fcdb8 the gate is 3m49s wall-clock, and in CI it shares\nbuild-grammars with -- and runs concurrently with -- a pytest step that took 935s\nin the same pipeline. The decision was taken against a number 2.6x too high; that\nis why this is a re-pricing rather than a reversal of someone's judgement.\n\nRESIDUAL, CARRIED BY INV-bozid, NOT BY THIS ITEM. The masking and addressing\ndefects are untouched here and are a class, not a property of this gate: one\naggregate status per workflow means a chronically-red step makes every sibling's\nverdict unreadable, and a cron verdict lands on a non-HEAD commit that\nscripts/ci-debug never reads. That applies to self-tree-validation,\ntest-agent-infra and all four nightly matrix legs. Its live cause -- the\nintermittent tracker TUI assertion that reddens the aggregate -- is WI-ruhul.\nNeither is a reason to hold this item open: this item's statement is about a\nself-claim regression reaching CI within a bounded number of commits, and it now\ndoes, through a path that does not route through the cron at all.\n\nNOT ESTABLISHED, said plainly: I did not identify which commit introduced the\noriginal regression. The pathlib surface rowing is most likely 12133e4ad0\n(2026-08-15), which PREDATES both arms existing -- the gate \"had been running\nnowhere\" until 097ab4e05a on 08-16 -- so on that reading the introducing commit\ncould not have been caught by any arm, and the three delivery defects are the\nwhole of what kept it hidden afterwards. I did not re-derive that attribution."  # fcd2
